 {:db/id "q-171998" :question/id #uuid "2fa1ebd9-8d46-5a04-b414-ffbaef5b882d" :question/math-academy-id "q-171998" :question/problem "$\\,$ $∃q\\in Q,\\,3q=2.$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the statement given above?" :question/worked-solution "The existential quantifier \"$∃$\" means \"there exists.\" So, our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $q\\in Q$ **such that** $3q=2.$ \n\nThis can be further simplified as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a rational number whose triple is $2.$\n\n**Note:** This statement is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-171998/ma-source-field/226182d462f77676d854c3ebe914d7048932afbacddd7f9cad2280bc56a11711"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
