 {:db/id "q-171999" :question/id #uuid "698421f5-96c5-5307-a8fb-d2ac4a250cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-171999" :question/problem "$\\,$ $∀x\\in (0,1),\\,x>{x}^{2}$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the statement given above?" :question/worked-solution "The universal quantifier \"$∀$\" means \"for all.\" So, our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $x\\in (0,1),\\,x>{x}^{2}.$\n\nThis can be further simplified as follows:\n\n$\\,$ Every number between $0$ and $1$ is greater than its square.\n\n**Note:** This statement is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-171999/ma-source-field/a85e7984a9e10b97545674ef1be7cfefe613387c2e9d202a3e31acce07e9e6e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
