 {:db/id "q-17392" :question/id #uuid "104d7814-9b21-55a2-864d-c61ec56f5c8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-17392" :question/problem "Given that $y=2{x}^{e}-ln⁡x$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{e}-ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e{x}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(2e{x}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2e\\cdot {1}^{e-1}-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =2e-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-17392/ma-source-field/1b44e0417b2ffc5c9cb56f94600d1c0765dbcb0f59624d1c544571c5d698a8db"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
