 {:db/id "q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405" :answer-field/id #uuid "948f7240-5694-5bc6-95db-83a3f04326f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405/1104276640c663181e306acd120e9f764816dcfc3af54a4fcf534b1136c2c0e3" "q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405/d866de91c02ba4f60133282b2fcb2578951b773cb3a3f0e10be0ae7679207377" "q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405/5ac8d31b66efca17d00d26bc5e7b06f25882593717f3b75d70c80bd7a591065a" "q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405/cbd7a18fd06e0a1333f757254cff4535d71f0fe57397d72ac58d6c87a00bad7a" "q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405/0367afafa42d47a9dd13f69f877b714fc54d89fcb6068970572f62761f0806cd"] :answer-field/correct "q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405/cbd7a18fd06e0a1333f757254cff4535d71f0fe57397d72ac58d6c87a00bad7a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "ffe3c5eb-c32b-557c-96a7-7ea03bab3fa8"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y+2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{x}\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1}\\,\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{z}^{-1}+2{x}^{2}{z}^{-2}}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{xz}+\\frac{2x}{{z}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{z}{x}-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{z}{x}-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-2x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-2x) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-2{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int 2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{3}}{3x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{3}}{3x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x}{C-2{x}^{3}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17544/ma-source-field/77c33e5cca8354f75c02c616fdd186fd8b1a64e6a4b1243743f037edfaedf405"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
