 {:db/id "q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e799e599-a900-5eac-8575-dfee31f5aa3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d/350618d9a0470d1bdf9251a0592c7a171742ffbc0c07c4a08666f35a51ca6719" "q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d/bc96103d8f143a7436bdbe3a5f7f985305e9fb4345f2423101a489d817024e1c" "q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d/9064cd80aef2f0af1ab76d93fb73ef31b601551498d0db5aaa675cb7257aceba" "q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d/1b4883a748983261d49fbb5c0772e5522146b2bf7f0089abbe601ed5fa82a10f" "q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d/ecaf5386391bbe4046dccea0f807cd58da122441d251057e5dc17968d5436273"] :answer-field/correct "q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d/bc96103d8f143a7436bdbe3a5f7f985305e9fb4345f2423101a489d817024e1c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "1ccfb013-777e-5e8a-8a81-f7a1a7ca50df"] :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{y(y-1)}{x}=0,\\,y(1)=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =x+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{x+C}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{x+C}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition  $y(1)=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =\\frac{1}{1+C}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{(x-\\frac{4}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{(5x-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17559/ma-source-field/fe5ba1054e9c39594f249af32704748f344a17a27474694820faf3583dd1264d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
