 {:db/id "q-176859" :question/id #uuid "e0f8781c-d297-5aca-886f-46748c33ed7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-176859" :question/problem "Given the statement\n\n$$\nP:0\\text{ is }\\text{not}\\text{ greater than }0.1\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following represents $¬P?$" :question/worked-solution "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n¬P:\\text{It is }\\text{not}\\text{ true that }0\\text{ is }\\text{not}\\text{ greater than }0.1,\n$$\n\n \n\nIn other words, $0$ is greater than $0.1.$ Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$$\n¬P:0\\text{ is greater than }0.1.\n$$\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-176859/ma-source-field/5aa1e97e5b9858b1d9c2e675e66abe1edb8dba1556a5dc6274d4058744cd5e46"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
