 {:db/id "q-177758" :question/id #uuid "7c55e65c-37f4-5fad-8b00-23ee3e7e21f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-177758" :question/problem "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is less than $2$ and it is rational.\"" :question/worked-solution "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is less than $2$ and it is rational\" with the phrase \"$x$ is rational and it is less than $2.$\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is rational and it is less than $2.$\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational, and it is less than $2.$\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational\" to just \"$x$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and it is less than $2.$\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and less than $2.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-177758/ma-source-field/0b9e08bd2d60668f0d82cc8316547bdf8324d78dc30de6cd6cf8347b52e7bf66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
