 {:db/id "q-177760" :question/id #uuid "fb50cec6-7c0e-563f-899c-48d469d6d9ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-177760" :question/problem "Simplify the following sentence: $x$ is even and it is an even number, or $x$ is even or it divides $11.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is even and it is an even number\" to just \"$x$ is even.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is even, or $x$ is even or it divides $11.$\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$x$ is even or $x$ is even, or it divides $11.$\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is even or $x$ is even\" to just \"$x$ is even.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is even, or it divides $11.$\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$x$ is even or it divides $11.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-177760/ma-source-field/69ba2759e47ce86da062280437b94e67db79b54a5fd00da55d71ca0ce9e7c425"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
