 {:db/id "q-183349" :question/id #uuid "2d8f44ce-e231-5920-980e-3c7663e37fa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-183349" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x\\in N,$ then  $x$ is positive.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in N.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183349/ma-source-field/9ddb1d345af2e316599253c64ad7f6e7e1da975015232ac0a04787ac38b66d38"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
