 {:db/id "q-183452" :question/id #uuid "030c3e29-d504-53d7-8a01-ca59114f9c38" :question/math-academy-id "q-183452" :question/problem "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $t\\in Q,$ $t<1.$" :question/worked-solution "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(t):t<1,\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀t\\in Q,\\,P(t).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n¬(∀t\\in Q,\\,P(t))≡∃t\\in Q,\\,¬P(t).\n$$\n\nFinally, $∃t\\in Q,\\,¬P(t)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $t\\in Q$ such that $t\\ge 1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183452/ma-source-field/6783fa0c880e831eede63adf6217a6de89f904514fb7c642d9c1fc812240f337"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
