 {:db/id "q-183515" :question/id #uuid "8238e2be-16fc-5278-bef2-5c7c9ad7976d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183515" :question/problem "$\\,$ $S(x):$ ${x}^{2}=3$\n\nGiven the predicate above, which of the following expresses the statement $∃x\\in Q,\\,S(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The existential quantifier \"$∃$\" means \"there exists.\" So, the statement \n$∃x\\in Q,\\,S(x)$ \nreads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $x\\in Q$ **such that** ${x}^{2}=3.$\n\n**Note:** This statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183515/ma-source-field/a0a002244fff8c1c9cd5a9f3c4e27341aaafd8ca26f191c1c931de7dbcc8aaf0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
