 {:db/id "q-183573" :question/id #uuid "090f259e-6817-5d8c-bd8b-c0774c7e3270" :question/math-academy-id "q-183573" :question/problem "$\\,$ $∀\\,ϵ\\in {R}^{+},\\,∃\\,x\\in Q,\\,-ϵ<x<ϵ.$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the statement given above?" :question/worked-solution "Our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $ϵ\\in {R}^{+},$ **there exists** $x\\in Q$ **such that** $-ϵ<x<ϵ.$ \n\nThis can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ Given any real number $ϵ>0$ there exists a rational number $x$ such that $-ϵ<x<ϵ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183573/ma-source-field/535199ce22d80fed9685e9d71cd31ed70d2b5ee23067e62752a908e4132f1769"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
