 {:db/id "q-183599" :question/id #uuid "f9724aea-cc2a-5bda-9ffa-87b9cd25835a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183599" :question/problem "$\\,$ $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,x+y=0$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the statement given above?" :question/worked-solution "Our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $x\\in R$ **such that**, **for all** $y\\in R,\\,x+y=0$ \n\nThis can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a real number $x$ such that $x+y=0$ for any real number $y.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183599/ma-source-field/be224d426ed520687c5d13b9a0fc90ef40b57be12f797ea3ba962caee7e32a87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
