 {:db/id "q-20362" :question/id #uuid "b5cb76d6-8596-56c0-bf91-5764390c6dbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-20362" :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+2z=1 \\\\ 3x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20362/ma-source-field/538f7e3b151612da3d118ef304fd0b59534ebce3204cf6980eb5d2afe706a282"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
